From d9f8558b4f0d6228de03273bf5b7b6b7c94a7e2a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Niluthon <37350260+Niluthon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 17:45:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/13] B70-0047: decode-aware expert ranking and a learned hot
 set that survives restarts

B70_MOE_HOTCOLD_SWAP_SOURCE=decode (with B70_MOE_ROUTE_COUNT=1) scores experts by the routes of the decode graphs
plus B70_MOE_HOTCOLD_SWAP_PREFILL_W (0.1) x the prefill routes, each normalised per layer and period: prefill
batches >= 512 tokens read the whole cold set from the 0042 VRAM slots, so only decode pays for a cold expert.
The route counter in the decode graphs is two kernels per layer (remainder + index_add_ from a static ones buffer)
instead of four; measured cost within noise (ms/step 49.5/59.1/47.9/45.5 vs 49.5/59.3/46.9/44.9).

B70_MOE_HOTCOLD_STATE=<prefix> keeps a long-term score per expert (decay B70_MOE_HOTCOLD_STATE_DECAY 0.999 per
active period, idle time does not decay it), writes <prefix>-rank<R>.json every B70_MOE_HOTCOLD_STATE_S (300) s;
the next boot places the hot set by it (checkpoint order as a 0.05 prior, B70_MOE_HOTCOLD_STATE_PRIOR) once it
holds B70_MOE_HOTCOLD_STATE_MIN_PERIODS (12) active periods, and seeds the short-term score with it.

Measured on 2x B70 (146 hot, 262K context, KV 279,001 unchanged), one run each: decode cold share in code agent
sessions 8-10 % -> 6-8 %; 12 sessions at 2 concurrent requests (adapted run) 94.1 -> 99.5 / 100.2 tok/s total;
general prompts after the code sessions 69.9 -> 113-115 tok/s at 4 streams; first requests after a restart with
the learned state 55.3 -> 60.7 tok/s mean at 1 stream.
